{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer aggregation with PCA_n2000 encoding in a multiprofile RNA-only setting, aiming to assess whether transformer aggregation's performance gains (observed with scvi_n200 encoder) are encoder-agnostic. Validation accuracy of 0.5191 (F1: 0.4797) is lower than the avgpool baseline (0.5907 accuracy) but higher than the singleprofile baseline (0.4849 accuracy), suggesting transformer aggregation may offer marginal benefits in multiprofile RNA-only settings. However, the result remains uncertain regarding its relative effectiveness compared to other aggregation methods and encoder-specific interactions."
}

